WEBVTT

1
00:00:40.246 --> 00:00:45.468
<i>The Pilgrim's Progress.
From this World to That Which is to Come,</i>

2
00:00:46.335 --> 00:00:49.214
<i>Delivered Under the Similitude of a Dream.</i>

3
00:00:51.632 --> 00:00:55.387
<i>Wherein is Discovered,
The Manner of His Setting Out,</i>

4
00:00:55.928 --> 00:00:57.680
<i>His Dangerous Journey</i>

5
00:00:58.556 --> 00:01:01.560
<i>And Safe Arrival at the Desired Country.</i>

6
00:01:51.817 --> 00:01:55.412
<i>As I walked through
the wilderness of this world,</i>

7
00:01:55.529 --> 00:01:58.954
<i>I lighted on a certain place
where was a den</i>

8
00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:02.787
<i>and I laid me down in that place to sleep.</i>

9
00:02:03.704 --> 00:02:07.208
<i>And as I slept, I dreamed a dream.</i>

10
00:02:09.084 --> 00:02:12.429
<i>I saw a man clothed with rags,</i>

11
00:02:12.588 --> 00:02:17.389
<i>standing in a certain place with
his face from his own house</i>

12
00:02:17.551 --> 00:02:21.852
<i>book in his hand,
and a great burden upon his back.</i>

13
00:02:25.643 --> 00:02:27.862
<i>All those years...</i>

14
00:02:29.938 --> 00:02:31.940
<i>living the life of someone...</i>

15
00:02:33.692 --> 00:02:35.239
<i>I didn't even know.</i>

16
00:03:04.014 --> 00:03:08.690
<i>Remember the story
I used to tell you when you were a boy...</i>

17
00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.113
<i>about a young prince.</i>

18
00:03:12.648 --> 00:03:14.696
<i>A knight,</i>

19
00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:18.286
<i>sent by his father, the King of the East,</i>

20
00:03:20.614 --> 00:03:22.161
<i>west into Egypt...</i>

21
00:03:26.578 --> 00:03:28.125
<i>to find a pearl.</i>

22
00:03:33.919 --> 00:03:37.014
<i>A pearl from the depths of the sea.</i>

23
00:03:47.474 --> 00:03:49.568
<i>But when the prince arrived,</i>

24
00:03:52.229 --> 00:03:56.075
<i>the people poured him a cup
that took away his memory.</i>

25
00:03:58.902 --> 00:04:01.200
<i>He forgot he was the son of the king.</i>

26
00:04:07.703 --> 00:04:09.455
<i>Forgot about the pearl...</i>

27
00:04:16.086 --> 00:04:18.384
<i>and fell into a deep sleep.</i>

28
00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:41.780
<i>The king didn't forget his son.</i>

29
00:04:43.947 --> 00:04:46.370
<i>He continued to send word...</i>

30
00:04:50.871 --> 00:04:52.418
<i>messengers...</i>

31
00:04:57.836 --> 00:04:59.634
<i>guides.</i>

32
00:05:03.383 --> 00:05:06.603
<i>But the prince... slept on.</i>

33
00:08:46.565 --> 00:08:49.034
<i>You see the palm trees?</i>

34
00:08:50.027 --> 00:08:52.405
<i>They tell you anything's possible.</i>

35
00:08:56.074 --> 00:08:57.621
<i>You can be anything...</i>

36
00:08:59.703 --> 00:09:01.250
<i>do anything...</i>

37
00:09:03.582 --> 00:09:05.129
<i>start over.</i>

38
00:09:09.004 --> 00:09:10.551
<i>You know?</i>

39
00:09:13.216 --> 00:09:17.062
I'm asking for your permission to make this

40
00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:20.269
a dramatic scene for one second...

41
00:09:44.247 --> 00:09:45.794
<i>My son...</i>

42
00:09:54.049 --> 00:09:55.596
<i>you are just like I am.</i>

43
00:10:01.681 --> 00:10:03.524
<i>Can't figure your life out?</i>

44
00:10:07.896 --> 00:10:09.990
<i>Can't put the pieces together?</i>

45
00:10:16.404 --> 00:10:18.406
<i>Just like me.</i>

46
00:10:26.456 --> 00:10:28.083
<i>A pilgrim on this earth.</i>

47
00:10:32.379 --> 00:10:33.926
<i>A stranger.</i>

48
00:10:57.195 --> 00:10:58.947
<i>Fragments...</i>

49
00:11:02.159 --> 00:11:03.706
<i>pieces...</i>

50
00:11:05.996 --> 00:11:07.543
<i>of a man.</i>

51
00:11:19.426 --> 00:11:21.724
<i>Where did I go wrong?</i>

52
00:12:01.092 --> 00:12:03.390
<i>What you wanna talk about?</i>

53
00:12:06.097 --> 00:12:08.316
You have nice eyes.

54
00:12:08.808 --> 00:12:10.355
Aren't I lucky.

55
00:12:10.936 --> 00:12:12.654
Where do you live?

56
00:12:12.812 --> 00:12:14.359
Why do ya wanna know?

57
00:12:15.649 --> 00:12:17.492
I want to write you a letter.

58
00:12:21.947 --> 00:12:24.416
What are you gonna say in your letter?

59
00:12:29.287 --> 00:12:31.665
Maybe you better not say it.

60
00:13:14.332 --> 00:13:17.962
<i>Let's live
like nobody's ever done it before.</i>

61
00:13:20.547 --> 00:13:21.594
<i>Wicked.</i>

62
00:13:21.756 --> 00:13:25.010
<i>Once the soul
was perfect and had wings...</i>

63
00:13:25.176 --> 00:13:26.519
<i>Brave.</i>

64
00:13:26.678 --> 00:13:32.060
<i>...it could soar into heaven
where only creatures with wings can be.</i>

65
00:13:32.267 --> 00:13:36.067
<i>But the soul lost its wings
and fell to Earth.</i>

66
00:13:36.229 --> 00:13:38.323
<i>There it took an earthly body.</i>

67
00:13:38.523 --> 00:13:41.367
<i>And now, while it lives in this body,</i>

68
00:13:41.526 --> 00:13:44.700
<i>no outward sign of wings can be seen.</i>

69
00:13:45.196 --> 00:13:47.995
<i>Yet the roots of its wings are still there.</i>

70
00:13:48.158 --> 00:13:51.833
<i>And the nature of wings is to try to raise
the earthbound body</i>

71
00:13:51.995 --> 00:13:53.747
<i>and soar with it into heaven.</i>

72
00:13:53.913 --> 00:13:58.919
<i>When we see a beautiful woman, or a man...</i>

73
00:13:59.502 --> 00:14:04.804
<i>the soul remembers the beauty
it used to know in heaven.</i>

74
00:14:05.425 --> 00:14:10.647
<i>And wings begin to spout,
and that makes the soul want to fly,</i>

75
00:14:10.805 --> 00:14:13.433
<i>but it cannot yet.
It is still too weak.</i>

76
00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:18.481
<i>So the man keeps staring up
into the sky like a young bird.</i>

77
00:14:18.646 --> 00:14:21.195
<i>He has lost
all interest in the world...</i>

78
00:14:21.941 --> 00:14:26.822
<i>- Can I come over?
- We just left each other.</i>

79
00:14:26.988 --> 00:14:28.706
<i>Are you alone?</i>

80
00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.997
<i>Of course.</i>

81
00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:37.712
On my phone sheet, I got agent
writers up my ass trying to get this job.

82
00:14:37.874 --> 00:14:42.095
<i>I just want to sit next to you.</i>

83
00:14:43.213 --> 00:14:46.342
Teddy thinks
you're the guy for this.

84
00:14:47.675 --> 00:14:50.770
That means the assignment
you didn't turn in, right,

85
00:14:50.929 --> 00:14:54.274
you don't have to worry about it.
Here's what happens. That goes away.

86
00:14:55.266 --> 00:14:59.271
<i>- What are you wearing?
- A dress.</i>

87
00:14:59.437 --> 00:15:02.190
- <i>What's it made of?
- How should I know?</i>

88
00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:04.947
<i>Cotton, I guess.</i>

89
00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:07.989
We said there's no way
you're gonna do it.

90
00:15:08.154 --> 00:15:11.749
So what'd we do? Said, double your quote.
And he did it.

91
00:15:12.242 --> 00:15:15.917
And that, Chuck signed off of that.
Teddy gets who he wants.

92
00:15:16.079 --> 00:15:18.173
The biggest comedy star wants you.

93
00:15:18.331 --> 00:15:22.757
Five years ago you came to me and
wanted to write big movies in Hollywood.

94
00:15:23.837 --> 00:15:27.216
- I mean...
- Okay, I don't want to see.

95
00:15:27.382 --> 00:15:31.558
Moments like this
don't come along, okay? This is it.

96
00:15:40.728 --> 00:15:42.822
<i>I see how you look at me.</i>

97
00:15:48.153 --> 00:15:50.622
<i>You think I could make you crazy?</i>

98
00:15:54.576 --> 00:15:56.670
<i>Crack you out of your shell?</i>

99
00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:06.967
<i>Make you suffer?</i>

100
00:16:29.944 --> 00:16:36.202
I... think... you're... weak.

101
00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:49.217
<i>You don't want love.</i>

102
00:16:55.261 --> 00:16:57.935
<i>You want a love experience.</i>

103
00:17:15.281 --> 00:17:17.283
Am I bringing you back to life?

104
00:17:28.294 --> 00:17:29.796
<i>Love and do what you like.</i>

105
00:17:33.633 --> 00:17:35.180
<i>A saint said that.</i>

106
00:17:41.808 --> 00:17:43.810
<i>Desire so deep.</i>

107
00:17:46.104 --> 00:17:47.697
<i>I'll throw my life away.</i>

108
00:17:50.191 --> 00:17:52.569
<i>Don't go back to being dead.</i>

109
00:18:03.454 --> 00:18:05.127
<i>What do you want?</i>

110
00:18:32.859 --> 00:18:36.113
We're not leading the lives
that we are meant for.

111
00:18:40.241 --> 00:18:42.744
We're meant for something else.

112
00:19:35.254 --> 00:19:38.224
My brother will translate.

113
00:19:55.108 --> 00:19:57.236
He looks around.

114
00:20:04.659 --> 00:20:07.412
He walks near the edge of the cliff.

115
00:20:28.099 --> 00:20:30.727
She says, like shadows.

116
00:20:42.405 --> 00:20:44.783
<i>Where will I meet you?</i>

117
00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:02.684
<i>Which way should I go?</i>

118
00:21:13.853 --> 00:21:15.855
<i>Suppose it isn't there for me,</i>

119
00:21:17.732 --> 00:21:19.279
<i>in the end?</i>

120
00:21:45.092 --> 00:21:46.639
<i>How do I begin?</i>

121
00:22:40.731 --> 00:22:42.574
<i>Remember how you showed up?</i>

122
00:22:43.985 --> 00:22:47.239
<i>Your wrists were taped up
like a tennis player's.</i>

123
00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:52.539
<i>You walked around
like nothing had happened.</i>

124
00:22:57.373 --> 00:23:01.298
<i>You were always doing it,
pretending everything was okay.</i>

125
00:23:03.087 --> 00:23:04.714
<i>But it wasn't.</i>

126
00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:19.904
- That's my brother, Rick.
- How are ya?

127
00:23:20.062 --> 00:23:23.282
What's goin' on, now? Anything.
Same today?

128
00:23:24.191 --> 00:23:28.367
Don't know how many times
I thought I'd die right here on the street.

129
00:23:29.614 --> 00:23:33.585
I picked him up and I had him
in my car, and a cop pulled us over.

130
00:23:33.701 --> 00:23:39.128
I tell him, "I'm a Methodist minister
and I'm looking after you, alright?"

131
00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:40.837
And I got off.

132
00:24:11.238 --> 00:24:16.460
<i>I dreamed that we were caught in
a huge tidal wave that engulfed the city.</i>

133
00:24:19.914 --> 00:24:23.168
<i>Any moment it seemed like
we might be swept under.</i>

134
00:24:26.545 --> 00:24:29.674
<i>There was a door
that I was afraid to go through.</i>

135
00:24:32.218 --> 00:24:35.973
<i>- I touched the knob...
- If I stuck you with a fork.</i>

136
00:24:37.974 --> 00:24:40.773
<i>Just wanna feel somethin', man.</i>

137
00:24:43.396 --> 00:24:45.319
<i>Wish we could do some things.</i>

138
00:24:47.108 --> 00:24:50.703
<i>Like goin' out on the Snake River together.
Remember?</i>

139
00:24:53.406 --> 00:24:55.579
<i>Think I'd end up here.</i>

140
00:24:58.911 --> 00:25:00.458
<i>Gracias.</i>

141
00:25:08.421 --> 00:25:10.765
It's good of you to invite me out here.

142
00:25:12.925 --> 00:25:15.678
Show me what it's like
to live a normal life.

143
00:25:24.395 --> 00:25:26.318
Somethin' wrong?

144
00:25:34.572 --> 00:25:36.119
What's up?

145
00:25:37.158 --> 00:25:40.412
I can tell when somethin's wrong, man.
I know you.

146
00:25:59.055 --> 00:26:01.683
What do you wanna talk about?

147
00:26:06.270 --> 00:26:09.524
I'm the only brother you got left.
You can tell me.

148
00:26:10.399 --> 00:26:11.946
I tell you stuff.

149
00:26:12.818 --> 00:26:14.912
<i>I loved my brother then.</i>

150
00:26:17.698 --> 00:26:19.245
<i>I hated him, too.</i>

151
00:26:21.702 --> 00:26:24.956
<i>For destroying everything
I'd been trying to do.</i>

152
00:26:25.956 --> 00:26:28.334
<i>To build us back up after Billy died.</i>

153
00:26:31.921 --> 00:26:37.223
I remember when they were putting Billy
in the ground, Dad went into hysterics.

154
00:26:38.761 --> 00:26:40.308
"My son!"

155
00:26:41.013 --> 00:26:42.560
Who fucking does that?

156
00:26:44.975 --> 00:26:47.194
<i>They said he took his life.</i>

157
00:26:48.896 --> 00:26:50.443
<i>But they don't know.</i>

158
00:26:54.693 --> 00:26:56.912
Oh, right now. Come on.

159
00:26:59.657 --> 00:27:01.204
I gotta feel something.

160
00:27:01.408 --> 00:27:02.955
<i>Like a snake.</i>

161
00:27:06.914 --> 00:27:08.461
<i>Swallowed him.</i>

162
00:27:09.625 --> 00:27:11.172
Come on, feel it.

163
00:27:19.009 --> 00:27:20.682
<i>Blind.</i>

164
00:27:25.015 --> 00:27:26.062
<i>Deaf.</i>

165
00:27:37.778 --> 00:27:39.325
<i>Grasping.</i>

166
00:27:40.114 --> 00:27:42.833
<i>I just wanted to twist a cane.</i>

167
00:27:46.996 --> 00:27:48.748
<i>Strike out, break free.</i>

168
00:27:50.791 --> 00:27:52.293
<i>Didn't have the guts.</i>

169
00:28:03.053 --> 00:28:04.976
<i>He's just an old fool.</i>

170
00:28:09.435 --> 00:28:11.813
<i>Just let him die with his blinders on.</i>

171
00:28:32.291 --> 00:28:34.134
<i>Redeem my life.</i>

172
00:28:38.505 --> 00:28:40.052
<i>Justify it.</i>

173
00:28:40.216 --> 00:28:45.393
<i>Ah, look at the fierce one.
The fierceness in his eyes. The rage!</i>

174
00:28:45.554 --> 00:28:47.852
...inflicted upon myself...

175
00:28:49.725 --> 00:28:51.272
<i>Oh Billy.</i>

176
00:28:54.521 --> 00:28:56.068
<i>I died.</i>

177
00:28:58.067 --> 00:28:59.614
<i>In a different way.</i>

178
00:29:06.325 --> 00:29:08.748
<i>I know you don't love me.</i>

179
00:29:14.208 --> 00:29:15.926
<i>I know things.</i>

180
00:29:16.085 --> 00:29:19.089
<i>- Say it.
- Serious information.</i>

181
00:29:22.675 --> 00:29:24.348
<i>I've blinded you.</i>

182
00:29:26.762 --> 00:29:28.309
<i>My life has...</i>

183
00:29:28.472 --> 00:29:31.726
I did every lousy, crappy job
that they wanted me to do.

184
00:29:31.892 --> 00:29:36.068
<i>But because I stumbled down
the road like a drunk...</i>

185
00:29:39.191 --> 00:29:41.660
<i>that doesn't mean it's the wrong one.</i>

186
00:29:58.627 --> 00:30:01.096
<i>I turned you upside down.</i>

187
00:30:07.011 --> 00:30:08.558
<i>My son.</i>

188
00:30:16.729 --> 00:30:19.699
<i>The light's gone out of your eyes.</i>

189
00:30:22.693 --> 00:30:24.240
<i>Womanizer.</i>

190
00:30:29.825 --> 00:30:31.372
<i>Cut off.</i>

191
00:31:22.503 --> 00:31:24.505
<i>Life.</i>

192
00:31:30.052 --> 00:31:31.599
<i>A goddess.</i>

193
00:32:43.625 --> 00:32:45.172
Angela...

194
00:32:48.797 --> 00:32:50.344
Frita...

195
00:32:50.507 --> 00:32:55.138
<i>Music is very important.
Helps me to fall in love.</i>

196
00:32:55.888 --> 00:32:57.731
<i>I fall in love 20 times a day.</i>

197
00:32:57.890 --> 00:33:01.815
Your face was very familiar to me, but I
didn't know from where. You're fantastic.

198
00:33:01.977 --> 00:33:03.149
Thank you.

199
00:33:03.312 --> 00:33:08.534
Listening to music on headsets, unaware you
are staring at them like a dirty ol' man.

200
00:33:09.401 --> 00:33:11.699
<i>Myself, I didn't wanna get a divorce.</i>

201
00:33:11.862 --> 00:33:16.208
I never stopped loving them.
But the way I loved them changed.

202
00:33:17.242 --> 00:33:18.494
<i>They are like flavors.</i>

203
00:33:18.660 --> 00:33:23.712
<i>Sometimes you want raspberry, then
after a while you want some strawberry.</i>

204
00:33:23.874 --> 00:33:26.878
- It's Abrasive.
- Oh, you are such a governor.

205
00:33:34.092 --> 00:33:35.935
- What's your name?
- Helen.

206
00:33:38.222 --> 00:33:39.769
What's your name?

207
00:33:40.432 --> 00:33:41.479
Rick.

208
00:33:41.600 --> 00:33:43.318
Do you know anybody here?

209
00:33:43.685 --> 00:33:46.063
No. Does that surprise you?

210
00:33:54.446 --> 00:33:56.369
- I know a guy.
- I know a guy...

211
00:33:57.199 --> 00:34:01.579
- ...like future space.
- You're at a party, it's alright.

212
00:34:21.431 --> 00:34:23.809
You know who'd be hot?
Cleopatra.

213
00:34:23.976 --> 00:34:26.775
If her nose had been this much shorter,

214
00:34:26.937 --> 00:34:29.031
it would've changed the world.

215
00:34:50.168 --> 00:34:51.715
<i>The Pearl.</i>

216
00:34:55.716 --> 00:34:57.263
<i>Somewhere in the sea.</i>

217
00:35:03.348 --> 00:35:04.895
<i>A chaos.</i>

218
00:35:10.897 --> 00:35:12.444
<i>Hungry.</i>

219
00:35:14.484 --> 00:35:16.612
<i>Longing for something other...</i>

220
00:35:20.824 --> 00:35:22.667
<i>without knowing what it is.</i>

221
00:35:32.127 --> 00:35:34.926
What about pink?
Do you like pink?

222
00:35:36.465 --> 00:35:42.973
- I love the company of women.
- It's pretty. Did it take long?

223
00:35:43.138 --> 00:35:46.108
<i>It seemed they knew something.</i>

224
00:35:46.266 --> 00:35:48.189
Some men don't like pink.

225
00:35:48.352 --> 00:35:52.778
- <i>But closer.</i>
- Now you tell me something.

226
00:35:54.900 --> 00:35:56.743
<i>To the mystery.</i>

227
00:36:07.996 --> 00:36:10.624
<i>Treat this world as it deserves.</i>

228
00:36:13.043 --> 00:36:14.886
<i>There are no principles...</i>

229
00:36:16.296 --> 00:36:17.843
<i>just circumstances.</i>

230
00:36:25.222 --> 00:36:26.769
<i>Nobody's home.</i>

231
00:36:26.932 --> 00:36:30.436
<i>Smoke machines in an empty sea.</i>

232
00:36:30.602 --> 00:36:32.195
<i>I got women in Tennessee.</i>

233
00:36:32.354 --> 00:36:36.655
<i>What can run but never walk,
some word have I found but never talk.</i>

234
00:36:36.775 --> 00:36:38.869
<i>Gonna take me out to see...</i>

235
00:36:57.921 --> 00:36:59.468
